  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9f2e8e5b57bd4bd99f33dd56077c2d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: KB_013_SpoolerStopped
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: POSTechSupport::POSTechSupport.Data.KnowledgeArticleSO
  articleId: KB-013
  title: Jobs queue up and never print
  category: 2
  content: "Paper present, driver healthy, jobs stacking up at 'Spooling' \u2014
    that combination is the Print Spooler service, not the printer. Windows accepts
    the job and then has nothing running to hand it over.\nCheck System \u25B8 Services
    for Print Spooler, restart it, and confirm with a test page. Work out this order
    before reinstalling anything: a driver reinstall (KB-002) will not start a stopped
    service, and you will have changed the machine for nothing."
  relatedErrorCodes: []
  guidanceForIssueIds:
  - P13
